T("Biology","Genetics and Punnett squares","Dominant, recessive and predicting traits","🧬","",
 ["Each parent passes on one allele for a gene. A dominant allele shows whenever it is present. A recessive allele shows only when there are two.", "The genotype is the pair of alleles, such as Bb. The phenotype is the trait you see.", "Meiosis makes four sex cells, each with half the usual number of chromosomes."],
 ["What do we call different forms of the same gene?|Alleles|Chromosomes|Gametes|Traits", "What is an organism with two identical alleles, such as BB, called?|Homozygous|Heterozygous|Hybrid|Haploid", "What is an organism with two different alleles, such as Bb, called?|Heterozygous|Homozygous|Purebred|Diploid", "What is the trait you can observe called?|Phenotype|Genotype|Allele|Karyotype", "Two Bb parents have a child. What is the chance the child is bb?|25%|50%|75%|0%", "A Bb parent and a bb parent have a child. What is the chance the child is bb?|50%|25%|75%|100%", "How many cells are made from one cell by meiosis?|Four|Two|One|Eight", "How many chromosomes are in a human sex cell?|23|46|92|2", "Who studied pea plants and is called the father of genetics?|Gregor Mendel|Charles Darwin|Louis Pasteur|James Watson", "In blood type AB, both alleles show fully. What is this called?|Codominance|Complete dominance|Recessiveness|Mutation"]);
