T("Physics","Forces and Newton's laws","F = m × a","🍎","",
 ["Newton's first law: an object keeps its motion unless a net force acts on it.", "Newton's second law: net force equals mass times acceleration.", "Newton's third law: for every action force there is an equal and opposite reaction force."],
 ["A 10 kg cart accelerates at 3 m/s². What is the net force?|30 N|13 N|3.3 N|7 N", "A 20 N net force acts on a 4 kg object. What is the acceleration?|5 m/s²|80 m/s²|16 m/s²|0.2 m/s²", "What is the weight of a 5 kg object on Earth? (g = 9.8 m/s²)|49 N|5 N|14.8 N|0.51 N", "A box is pushed right with 10 N and left with 4 N. What is the net force?|6 N to the right|14 N to the right|6 N to the left|14 N to the left", "Which law explains why you move forward when a bus stops suddenly?|Newton's first law|Newton's second law|Newton's third law|The law of gravitation", "A swimmer pushes water backward and moves forward. Which law is this?|Newton's third law|Newton's first law|Newton's second law|Ohm's law", "What is the tendency of an object to resist changes in motion called?|Inertia|Friction|Momentum|Weight", "What is the support force a surface pushes up with called?|Normal force|Friction|Tension|Gravity", "If the net force on an object is zero, what is true?|Its velocity is constant|It must be at rest|It speeds up|It slows down", "What is the unit of mass?|Kilogram|Newton|Joule|Metre per second"]);
T("Physics","Work, energy and power","Joules and watts","🔋","",
 ["Work is force times distance and is measured in joules.", "Kinetic energy is one half times mass times speed squared. Gravitational potential energy is mass times g times height.", "Power is work divided by time and is measured in watts. Energy is never created or destroyed. It only changes form."],
 ["A 50 N force moves a box 4 m. How much work is done?|200 J|12.5 J|54 J|46 J", "What is the kinetic energy of a 2 kg ball moving at 3 m/s?|9 J|6 J|18 J|3 J", "What is the potential energy of a 2 kg book 5 m above the floor? (g = 9.8 m/s²)|98 J|10 J|49 J|16.8 J", "A motor does 600 J of work in 3 s. What is its power?|200 W|1800 W|603 W|0.005 W", "What is the unit of energy?|Joule|Watt|Newton|Volt", "What is the unit of power?|Watt|Joule|Newton|Ampere", "A machine takes in 120 J and gives 30 J of useful energy. What is its efficiency?|25%|40%|75%|90%", "What does the law of conservation of energy say?|Energy cannot be created or destroyed|Energy is always lost|Energy is created by motion|Energy only exists as heat", "As a ball falls, what happens to its energy?|Potential energy changes to kinetic energy|Kinetic energy changes to potential energy|All of its energy disappears|Its energy doubles", "If speed doubles, what happens to kinetic energy?|It becomes four times as large|It doubles|It stays the same|It halves"]);

